{"name":"Guo Tie Dumpling","hex":"#bd7e08","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"guo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Guayabero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guo"},{"term":"tie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knot; a fastening.","A knot of hair, as at the back of a wig."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To twist (a string, rope, or the like) around itself securely.","To form (a knot or the like) in a string or the like."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tie"},{"term":"dumpling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ball of dough that is cooked and may have a filling and/or additional ingredients in the dough. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n Specifically, a ball of dough used in stews and other sauced dishes; a thick noodle.\n Specifically, a food composed of a dough wrapper around a filling.","Specifically, a ball of dough used in stews and other sauced dishes; a thick noodle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumpling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Guo","blocks":[{"text":"\"Guo\", written in Chinese: 郭, is one of the most common Chinese surnames and means \"the wall that surrounds a city\" in Chinese. It can also be transliterated as Cok, Gou, Quo, Quach, Quek, Que, Keh, Kuo, Kwo, Kuoch, Kok, Koc, Kwee, Kwek, Kwik, Kwok, Kuok, Kuek, Gock, Koay, or Ker. The Korean equivalent is spelled Kwak; the Vietnamese equivalent is Quách."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/%E9%83%AD%E5%A7%93_-_%E6%A5%B7%E9%AB%94.svg/330px-%E9%83%AD%E5%A7%93_-_%E6%A5%B7%E9%AB%94.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guo","wikidata":"Q4140836"},{"title":"Dumpling","blocks":[{"text":"Dumplings are a broad class of dishes that consist of pieces of cooked dough, often wrapped around a filling. The dough can be based on bread, wheat or other flours, or potatoes, and it may be filled with meat, fish, tofu, cheese, vegetables, or a combination. Dumplings may be prepared using a variety of cooking methods and are found in many world cuisines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/HK_SYP_%E8%A5%BF%E7%87%9F%E7%9B%A4_Sai_Ying_Pun_Kwan_Yick_Building_%E5%90%8D%E6%98%9F%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%85%92%E5%AE%B6_Star_Seafood_Restaurant_food_%E5%90%9E%E9%BA%B5_Wonton_dim_sum_October_2020_SS2_01.jpg/330px-HK_SYP_%E8%A5%BF%E7%87%9F%E7%9B%A4_Sai_Ying_Pun_Kwan_Yick_Building_%E5%90%8D%E6%98%9F%E6%B5%B7%E9%AE%AE%E9%85%92%E5%AE%B6_Star_Seafood_Restaurant_food_%E5%90%9E%E9%BA%B5_Wonton_dim_sum_October_2020_SS2_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dumpling","wikidata":"Q1854639"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Pelmeni_Russian.jpg/500px-Pelmeni_Russian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Pelmeni_Russian.jpg/1280px-Pelmeni_Russian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Pelmeni_Russian.jpg/500px-Pelmeni_Russian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APelmeni_Russian.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/04565_Christmas_dumplings_with_dried_plums.JPG/500px-04565_Christmas_dumplings_with_dried_plums.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/04565_Christmas_dumplings_with_dried_plums.JPG/500px-04565_Christmas_dumplings_with_dried_plums.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3